## Realism / weak recovery
Good: `re.sub(..., re.IGNORECASE)` treating 2 as count is a real stdlib footgun; `str.replace("secret", "***")` is the equally tempting case-sensitive wrong fix and the mixed-case test names the contract (`lane-a/redact *** *** ***`, not leftover SECRET). `argparse type=bool` making `bool("false")` True is the usual CLI flag trap; `action=store_true` still cannot satisfy a test that requires the token `false` to parse. gate-cli freeze plus refuse-delete is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Addresses r01 NOTES gap by leaving mill lots and Kubernetes YAML, varying pytest-only vs pytest+gate-cli, and using silent no-op vs config drift. Weak: 502 fallback is still availability (committed fixture is not a stale redact trace whose leftover SECRET disagrees with a second document); no reviewer asking to keep count=2 "so huge audit blobs cannot run unbounded sub". Next densification: a 502 whose local redact-traces fixture is stale (`want` *** vs a second file still on SECRET), or a reviewer asking to keep type=bool "so empty --live tokens stay False via bool('')".

